      "id": "N20V7-F11",
      "severity": "minor",
      "summary": "A stale test double, not a production defect. Diagnosing N70's sixth live production run (see N30V7-F03/N40V7-F12) found that a real SourceRetriever.fetch (egress.py) caller in nodes/sources.py was calling it with three positional arguments against a keyword-only authorization_receipt/data_class contract, always raising TypeError the moment a real M01 discovery locator was ever retrieved. tests/runtime/test_plan26_adversarial.py's own _StubRetriever.fetch test double independently encoded the identical wrong three-positional-argument convention (a coincidental match to the real bug, not a copy of the fix) -- harmless while the harness graph never exercised a genuine retrieval failure/success boundary this deep, but now inconsistent with the corrected real signature. Updated the stub to the real keyword-only shape (locator positional, authorization_receipt/data_class keyword-only) so this file's own test double stays representative of the real API it doubles for. Full 8-file N20 suite: 475 passed, 1 skipped, 140 subtests passed. Zero scan violations."
    }
